  "title": "Chroma Heatmap",
  "caption": "The 12 chroma bins over the first 6 seconds of D1_training-e_e02008 (PhysioNet 2016, 17.6 s). Chroma is a musical-pitch construct with no physiological meaning for heart sounds; it is used here purely as a generic harmonic-distribution descriptor. The colour scale spans the actual range rather than a nominal 0-1, because the real dynamic range on this corpus is narrow and that flatness is itself the point.",
